e to development  issues but still the players at the time  didn't know that halo 2 was going to get  a sequel and they thought this is all  they were left with this is the same for  halo infinite will halo infinite get a  sequel absolutely there is no doubt in  my mind that it will so there's going to  be some new story content except we  don't know when some people have stated  halo infinite is supposed to be a  10-year game assuming this is true then  we'll either have to wait 10 years for a  new story or wait until the dlc if there  even is dlc the problem is that neither  option is confirmed halo infinite might  be a 10-year game but maybe it's just  for multiplayer there's nothing stopping  them from shafting the single-player  fans and making them wait a decade for  new content the fact that the time frame  is that long though is what leads people  to believe that story dlc will be coming  out for this game which if that's the  case and this entire argument is  redundant i only feel this way about the  game's story because who knows how long  it'll be until the next installment but  if dlc is currently something 343 is  looking into then i'm all for it as this  story is really something and it needs  to be explored as soon as possible the  other criticism i've seen is about  cortana and how it was never shown to  the player how she managed to lose her  influence despite being incredibly  powerful and the fact that they killed  her off using a flashback while i agree  it's maybe not the greatest way to go  about it i think it's 343's attempt at  trying to push her away from us the way  that cortana is pushing the master chief  away from her so that he can focus on  the future is how 343 is treating us i  feel like this is what they always  wanted to do with cortana as this is  what occurred in halo 4. the problem is  that they wrote themselves into a corner  which led into halo 5 but after some  time they eventually regained their  footing and committed to it 