 the same as they both snapped their  fingers now i tried to look through all  my footage of the halo games which is  easily over 20 hours of footage so it  would take a lot of time to actually  sift through it all but i don't recall  cortana ever actually snapping her  fingers even in the 343 games i don't  remember her doing this i feel like this  was something that was just added into  halo infinite as a way to show how the  weapon and cortana are the same going  back to the weapon she is master chief's  new ai and new ally she obviously cares  about him and wants to help him but  despite all her efforts he still doesn't  trust her when the two are working  together to take down the spires we see  that the weapon is being scanned by  something we don't know what however  that's not a good sign master chief then  prepares this deactivation program so  that he can delete the weapon he's going  to outright delete her at the first sign  of trouble despite cortana being stuck  on high charity with the gravemind and  actively trying to harm him throughout  halo 4 and 5 whether intentional or not  he always refused to delete her and  wants to fix her because the chief cares  about her but because the only person he  truly cares about is gone now he stopped  caring about those around him both the  pilot and weapon were just seen as  things he can use the weapon after this  becomes rightfully upset with him as she  learns that he tried to delete her the  two end up getting into an argument  about it and he tries to convince her  that he was trying to stop her from  putting the mission at risk but once  again cortana has been in worse  situations and he never thought of  deleting her despite all of this she  still continues to work with him as she  understands that the mission is very  important and it's not worth  compromising the mission over their  relationship during their down time when  things aren't going on is when she finds  it appropriate to bring it back up again  their one engagement shortly after this  was also a hint towards cortana and the  weapon being one in the same as when  they argue he says cortana's name i  trusted you why can't you do the same  you don't understand try me cortana  judging from the pause in between his  sentence it seems that since the weapon  and cortana are the same he got them  mixed up and ended up saying her name  instead i'm not entirely sure if the  player was supposed to interpret it this  way but that's what i got from it and it  makes the showcase of their relationship  and the build-up to that reveal much  better as i said earlier the weapon and  the pilot are just things he can use in  his mission this also relates to their  names they are things not actual names  he also never calls them the weapon or  the pilot we the player just call them  that it's on until the end of the game  where he finally learns both their names  which is showing how the master chief is  thinking of them as real people not just  a role in his mission the weapon isn't  just a weapon used to destroy the  banished and the pilot isn't just a  pilot taking him to places he needs to  go they're real people to him and people  he cares about and wants to protect in  the beginning the relationship felt  forced and shaky between the three but  by the end they feel like a well-oiled  machine each serving a role on the team  and realizing that despite each of their  faults they're just as equally important  as the other and this goes back to what  i was talking about earlier how 343 is  trying to humanize the chief now they're  keeping with the theme of him being an  unstoppable force but they're showing  his flaws and mistakes and it's these  mistakes that inspire those around him  it's some fantastic storytelling and a  wonderful experience to see unfold  however this is just one part of the  overall story the other side of the  story is with the banished and right out  of the gate to the banister a fantastic  faction i've always been a fan of the  covenant but the prometheans just worked  my cup of tea because it felt too sci-fi  for halo i know how crazy that sounds  given the technology of this game but i  don't mind the alien looking species  like the covenant or even the harbinger  but the mechanical nature of the  prometheans just never sat right with me  like i said i understand how potentially  hypocritical that may sound but that's  just my opinion regardless the banished  seem to scratch my itch perfectly as  they closely resemble the covenant but  aren't an actual copy it allows the  enemies in combat to feel familiar but  also feel new at the same time but the  banister aren't great just from a  gameplay perspective but also from a  story one as well they feel strong and  we get to see that right in the opening  minutes it makes the story all the more  engaging as it's not a story of the  master chief defeating the covenant for  the millionaire's time him losing  signifies that these enemies are  stronger than we think and that things  can go wrong and we might end up getting  the bad ending by the time we reach the  epilogue as for the characters  themselves the three main pillars of the  faction being atriox escherim and jega  are all fantastic i was really upset  that they killed jewel mandama off right  away in halo 5 as i felt like there  wasn't enough time spent with him even  though we did get to see him quite  substantially in spartan ops with these  three i was eagerly waiting for them to  show up even when ashram said that  atriox was dead i wasn't bothered by  this as i was with joule mujul mendama  dead there really wasn't much point to  the covenant existing anymore and the  game sort of knew this as they did away  with the covenant for most of the game  and really tried to focus on the  prometheans and cortana but with halo  infinite atriox being dead means nothing  as jega and ashram still exist and will  take his place we don't hear about a  successor to jewel's role as supreme  commanders you could stop caring about  the covenant altogether and it makes it  feel like they already lost but with  atriax dead it still feels like the  banish have the upper hand despite  losing their warmaster this was a much  better way of killing a character early  in the game without ruining the  integrity of the story now obviously  this is made even better when we  discover atriox isn't actually dead but  we'll get to that later voltage and  escheron both have roles and  personalities that are only distinct  from one another but it's these exact  qualities that make them likable  antagonists i couldn't wait to finally  fight jega as he was such an anomaly  within this faction and i couldn't wait  to see what would happen when we  actually did meet him these cutscenes we  see from them also bring up another  point i've been meaning to mention but  it's that this game is gorgeous i've  always liked the sort of realistic  graphics of halo 3 in reach but just  like the prometheans the hyper realism  of halo 4 and 5 just felt too much to me  master chief's armor just had too much  detail going on but infinite nails the  perfect blend of this i've seen a lot of  complaints about this game downgrading  its graphics but in this case it  actually makes the game better this also  extends to the banished as their visual  design is fantastic and with a change in  their color palette it allows them to  further separate from the covenant  making them feel new going back to the  banished i think both jega and ashram  are standout characters within the game  as while they just want to kill the  master chief the characters themselves  are different than that ashram  constantly wants to challenge the chief  and he is eagerly waiting for the time  they stand in front of one another the  jega the master chief is just another  spartan he's killed tons before so how  is this any different jega's boss fight  is easily one of the best in the game as  the chief is tasked with going through  this arena of torture before being stuck  in a tiny room with two floors no lights  and barely any cover to top it off jega  has active camo and two energy swords  not only does he look cool but this  fight is nerve-racking thanks to the  huge buff that activecamo got in halo  infinite it is so hard to see where an  enemy is unless you're standing still  this leaves you exposed to the active  camo user making the fight even harder  plus the energy swords are just as  deadly as before it's a fantastic fight  and it gets even better once you get  introduced to ashram as he is kitted  with full armor and is ready to fight  even as a second phase where he chases  you with his gravity hammer i have never  felt more stressed in this game than i  have here and it's the story and their  personalities that made this enjoyable  jager being a spartan killer was huge  this could be the first time in a while  where we feel like the opponent we face  is on an even playing field with us and  with eshroom you could tell just from  his attitude that this was going to be a  very tough fight ashram loves the  feeling of battle so it makes sense how  he gets excited when we finally come  face to face with him there's no  gimmicks with him there's no cheap  tactics like with jega it's just a test  of metal as he puts it this is probably  why he made jega fight the chief first  as esheram holds jega to a very high  esteem so if the spartan can kill a  spartan killer then this will be a  battle for the ages this fight is what  esheram has been waiting for no one in  the unsc is as tough as the chief so if  ashram can defeat him he'll be a living  legend and praised forever i was so  engaged in these battles not because of  how tough they are but what they meant  which is why i felt it'd be poetic for  ashram to die by the weapon of his  friend the moment after his defeat was  also just wonderful even though he lost  he still won't stop until the chief  kills him or he becomes victorious the  chief also respects him during his death  which is something he hasn't done before  ashram and the chief are one and the  same just soldiers in a war hoping they  do the right thing and seeing as they're  on a leveled playing field in regards to  their skill he wanted to show him a sign  of respect it was honestly quite  touching and something i didn't expect  the chief to do considering how many  other covenant foes he's killed  throughout the franchise if it wasn't  obvious from how long i've discussed  these characters the banish the pilot  and the weapon are incredibly unique and  wonderful additions to this game the  chief was also given more human emotions  giving the chief the opportunity to  evolve as a character and even giving  others around him the chance to evolve  but these characters are just part of  the overall story as we still have yet  to talk about halo infinite's  overarching narrative halo infinite is  about the master chief learning to  accept his new fate and continuing to  work and care for those people around  him and it's because of cortana that  this happened he finally has to come to  terms with her death and accepts that he  can't change the past but he can change  the future he failed to stop cortana but  he won't fail his new friends that's  what caused him to reflect on his own  actions like his dismissive attitude  towards the pilot or how he just sees  the weapon as a weapon to fight the  banished what ties all these characters  and narrative evolutions together is  this ongoing plot with atriox cortana  and the harbinger we learn from the  echoes of cortana that she is to blame  for so many atrocities that have  occurred she's completely destroyed  sydney australia blew up laconia station  and erased the banished homeworld right  in front of atriox's eyes not only was  the reveal of these events really well  done i liked that it was able to  showcase the motivations behind atriox  as of the harbinger she's interesting to  say the least she's of a completely new  species so this is already captivating  enough as this could lead to more story  regarding her species which is most  likely where this game is gonna head but  the harbinger throughout the game will  continue to talk about the endless this  unknown faction or group that we the  player don't even know of yet her goal  is separate from the banished and i do  appreciate the detail of them working  together to achieve their goal but not  actually working together they don't  hate each other but they definitely  don't trust one another but they need to  in order to get their way it establishes  different motivations and different  personalities between the characters and  that it was just an overall great  addition to the game what did bother me  at least initially was how quickly she  fades out of the game's existence she's  introduced in the middle of the game and  is gone by the end however given her  name the harbinger i didn't feel that  way anymore as a harbinger is someone or  something that announces the approach of  something else her motivations and goals  are all based around the textbook  definition of her name after realizing  this i didn't feel as bad that she died  so soon as i became more interested in  what was to come after her death what  exactly that is remains unknown but  numerous theories have already been  started as the post-credit cutscene of  halo infinite shows us that atriox is  still alive but in a different point in  time he seems to have time traveled back  in time for some reason we also hear two  people speaking during the legendary  ending which is someone called the great  edict and then despondent pyre who we  already know of but more importantly  it's the fact that offensive bias is  being activated now i'll be the first to  admit most of my halo knowledge comes  from the games with only the smallest  amount of info being outside sources so  i knew who they were talking about but  someone who has never read the books  will not but i don't mind this halo  infinite really feels like a game for  those who have played the prior releases  it's quite the hard game to jump into as  a first-time halo player so this ending  was really for the fans the ones who  know who offensive bias is and what this  could mean for the future the main  question of course is how atriox went  back in time and it ties into the  harbinger and the endless who people  assumed to be the precursors once again  people who don't know what the  precursors are will be scratching their  head at these theories but halo infinite  is for the dedicated players it creates  some intrigue in new players as while  these names and factions can be a bit  overwhelming they're still very  interesting and it also creates  excitement in the veteran players as  they know the lore and are excited as  different pieces of the overall universe  are finally being put into the games  from start to finish this game was  incredible however i do have some issues  with the game but it's issues that can  be fixed my biggest issue and it's the  issue lots of people in my comments  section of my video were talking about  was cortana's death and the story's  length despite being an open world game  if you were to just play its story it's  just as long as any other halo game i  beat it on my first playthrough in about  6 hours obviously this is a weird thing  to critique but given that all the story  is within the main content and not open  world activities it's really just a  regularly sized halo game without the  feeling of completion once the credits  rolled the story's done and when they  did roll i felt like we were just  getting started we got introduced to the  harbinger the endless and atriox going  back in time yet it just ends this was  something the original game struggled  with especially with halo 2 as nothing  felt accomplished obviously with that  game that was more due to development  issues but still the players at the time  didn't know that halo 2 was going to get  a sequel and they thought this is all  they were left with this is the same for  halo infinite will halo infinite get a  sequel absolutely there is no doubt in  my mind that it will so there's going to  be some new story content except we  don't know when some people have stated  halo infinite is supposed to be a  10-year game assuming this is true then  we'll either have to wait 10 years for a  new story or wait until the dlc if there  even is dlc the problem is that neither  option is confirmed halo infinite might  be a 10-year game but maybe it's just  for multiplayer there's nothing stopping  them from shafting the single-player  fans and making them wait a decade for  new content the fact that the time frame  is that long though is what leads people  to believe that story dlc will be coming  out for this game which if that's the  case and this entire argument is  redundant i only feel this way about the  game's story because who knows how long  it'll be until the next installment but  if dlc is currently something 343 is  looking into then i'm all for it as this  story is really something and it needs  to be explored as soon as possible the  other criticism i've seen is about  cortana and how it was never shown to  the player how she managed to lose her  influence despite being incredibly  powerful and the fact that they killed  her off using a flashback while i agree  it's maybe not the greatest way to go  about it i think it's 343's attempt at  trying to push her away from us the way  that cortana is pushing the master chief  away from her so that he can focus on  the future is how 343 is treating us i  feel like this is what they always  wanted to do with cortana as this is  what occurred in halo 4. the problem is  that they wrote themselves into a corner  which led into halo 5 but after some  time they eventually regained their  footing and committed to it now that  they have the weapon the banished and  the endless to explore so i really don't  mind that she's dead and i also don't  mind how it was presented as it goes  back to what i said before cortana  doesn't want to meddle in the chief's  life anymore that was the whole point of  her message at the end of the game she  has this poison that the chief can't let  go of but now that she's officially dead  she thinks this will allow the chief to  stop looking at the past and move on in  this instance we are the chief cortana  is gone and we have to accept that and  the more they put her on screen the more  we start to care about her and less  about the characters within that new  game despite how incredible and iconic  she is we need to move on halo  infinite's campaign was fantastic and is  without a doubt the best game 343 has  ever made its story was well constructed  so that everything fit where it needed  to within the game's world and it was  intriguing enough that it made me want  to see what would come next halo  infinite is not the best game in the  series but given how halo 4 and 5 were  presented this was a huge breath of  fresh air for the franchise with that  being said though we have come to the  end of the video thank you for watching  and making it this far i really enjoyed  making this story review and it's  something i've been wanting to do for a  lot of other games for a while so be on  the lookout for that kind of content in  the future as always like the view if  you enjoyed and subscribe if you're new  if you want to see more halo content  like this i made a retrospective review  on the main entries in the series and i  also made a recap of halo infinite's  story in case things got confusing be on  the lookout for more content like this  in the near future for many other games  and of course thank you to my returning  viewers for coming back to another video  take care everyone  and goodbye  [Music]  you
 

